From 21b27d70c8becfec322234bc6109fd1d285c330d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 00:28:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0252 -- gus (#39 probe): log SetHint ret + immediate
 readback in bridge

TEMPORARY diagnostic (revert after triage). The 0251 bridge builds + embeds all
hint strings, but GUS_DIAG still does not resolve at the SDL read point under
DOSBox-X, and the SDL source trace says by-source it SHOULD -- a runtime
behavior we can't model statically. Go empirical: in the _gus_passthru loop,
right after each SDL_SetHintWithPriority(name, v, OVERRIDE), log BOTH the bool
return AND an immediate same-name SDL_GetHint readback (pre-SDL_Init).

ALWAYS-ON (not GUS_DIAG-gated -- GUS_DIAG is the broken hint). One capture
decides:
- readback==value + ret=true -> the table HAS the hint right after the bridge,
  so a later-null at the SDL read point is a loss ACROSS SDL_Init (-> sdl-pg
  gus-11 SDL-read-point probe).
- readback null / ret=false -> SetHintWithPriority didn't take -> bridge-level
  bug (try plain SDL_SetHint to match the working ULTRASND call).

Engine-only, zero SDL rebuild. Default behavior otherwise unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/main.cpp | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index 1f0dd5ba..60e3ac5e 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -1690,7 +1690,18 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
       const char *v = std::getenv(_gus_passthru[i]);
       if (v && v[0] != '\0')
       {
-        SDL_SetHintWithPriority(_gus_passthru[i], v, SDL_HINT_OVERRIDE);
+        // patch 0252 (#39 / task#43 probe, ALWAYS-ON -- NOT GUS_DIAG-gated,
+        // since GUS_DIAG is the hint that fails to resolve): log the SetHint
+        // bool return + an IMMEDIATE same-name SDL_GetHint readback, right here
+        // pre-SDL_Init. Decisive: readback==value+ret=true -> the table HAS it
+        // after the bridge (so any later null is a loss ACROSS SDL_Init ->
+        // sdl-pg gus-11 read-point probe); readback null / ret=false -> the
+        // SetHint itself didn't take (bridge-level bug). Revert after triage.
+        bool _ret = SDL_SetHintWithPriority(_gus_passthru[i], v, SDL_HINT_OVERRIDE);
+        const char *_rb = SDL_GetHint(_gus_passthru[i]);
+        LOG_INFO("GUS-BRIDGE-PROBE: SetHint('{}','{}') ret={} readback='{}'",
+                 _gus_passthru[i], v, _ret ? "true" : "false",
+                 _rb ? _rb : "(null)");
         ++_nbridged;
       }
     }
